  "kind": "bughunt",
  "starterShould": "runtime_error:use_after_free",
  "params": [{"name": "initial", "type": "int[]"}, {"name": "values", "type": "int[]"}],
  "examples": [
    {"input": ["[1,2,3]", "[4,5]"], "output": "[1,2,3,4,5]", "explanation": "The harness puts [1,2,3] in a malloc'd array, then calls arr = appendValue(arr, &size, v) for 4 and for 5."},
    {"input": ["[]", "[7]"], "output": "[7]"}
  ],
  "hints": [
    "Run it: the report says the write hit a block that was \"moved by realloc()\".",
    "realloc may move the block. Where is the new block, and what happens to the old one?",
    "Use realloc's return value, and keep the old pointer until you know realloc succeeded."
  ],
  "constraints": ["0 <= initial length, values length <= 1000"],
  "memory": "Return the array's current address (it may have moved). The caller frees it at the end."
}
@@ description
`appendValue` adds one element to the end of a heap array and returns the array.

```c
int *appendValue(int *arr, int *size, int value);
```

It is used like this:

```c
int size = 3;
int *arr = malloc(3 * sizeof *arr);   /* ... filled with data ... */
arr = appendValue(arr, &size, 4);
arr = appendValue(arr, &size, 5);
free(arr);
```

On the developer's machine it worked perfectly for small arrays and crashed for big ones. **Find and fix the bug.**

LeakCode's `realloc` *always* moves the block (a real allocator does so only when it can't grow it in place), so code that depends on the block staying put fails every time instead of only occasionally.
@@ prelude
int *appendValue(int *arr, int *size, int value);
@@ starter
#include <stdlib.h>

int *appendValue(int *arr, int *size, int value) {
    realloc(arr, (*size + 1) * sizeof *arr);
    arr[*size] = value;
    (*size)++;
    return arr;
}
@@ solution
#include <stdlib.h>

int *appendValue(int *arr, int *size, int value) {
    int *bigger = realloc(arr, (*size + 1) * sizeof *arr);
    if (bigger == NULL) return arr;     /* out of memory: arr is untouched and still valid */
    bigger[*size] = value;
    (*size)++;
    return bigger;
}
@@ driver
#include "lc_driver.h"

int main(void)
{
    while (lc_next_case()) {
        int n, m, i, size;
        int *init = lc_read_int_array(&n);
        int *vals = lc_read_int_array(&m);
        int *arr = (int *)malloc((size_t)n * sizeof *arr);
        for (i = 0; i < n; i++) arr[i] = init[i];
        size = n;
        for (i = 0; i < m; i++) arr = appendValue(arr, &size, vals[i]);
        if (size != n + m) lc_fail("size is %d after %d appends to %d elements.", size, m, n);
        lc_out_int_array(arr, size);
        LC_FREE_RESULT(arr, "the array returned by appendValue()");
        lc_end_case();
    }
    return lc_finish();
}
@@ tests
